<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Minnesota</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Minnesota is a state in the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midwestern-united-states">Midwest</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> and Lake Superior, with its capital at Saint Paul. It holds the headwaters of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> and was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the Dakota and later also of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ojibwe">Ojibwe</a>. American settlement grew after treaties in the 1850s, it became a state in 1858, and the Dakota War of 1862 led to the expulsion of most Dakota from the state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/minnesota.jpg" alt="Minnesota" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Minnesota State Emblems Redesign Commission Vector: Jamie Eilat, Undertiago · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Minnesota.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
